msgid "Unfinished: `warning[unfinished] ...`; it produces no theorem authority, but checking continues with the following theorems."
msgstr "未完成：`warning[unfinished] ...`，不会产生 theorem authority，但会继续检查后续 theorem。"

#: manual/syntax.md:307
msgid "The `--` in `moon run src/cmd -- -d --no-warn <file>` belongs only to `moon run` argument forwarding; a standalone executable does not need it, so run `qed-cmd -d --no-warn <file>` directly."
msgstr "`moon run src/cmd -- -d --no-warn <file>` 中的 `--` 只属于 `moon run` 参数转发；独立可执行文件不需要它，直接用 `qed-cmd -d --no-warn <file>`。"

#: manual/syntax.md:310
msgid "See [User manual](manual.md) for the complete failure fields, unfinished fields, and stable examples."
msgstr "更完整的失败字段、unfinished 字段和稳定示例见 [用户手册](manual.md)。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:1
msgid "cmd tutorial"
msgstr "cmd 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:3
msgid "This tutorial checks theorem-script files with the command-line tool `qed-cmd`. You run the examples shipped in `examples/`, read successes, errors and unfinished proofs, and use the exit status in scripts. No MoonBit code is needed."
msgstr "本教程使用命令行工具 `qed-cmd` 检查定理脚本文件。你将运行 `examples/` 中自带的示例，读懂成功、错误和未完成证明的输出，并在脚本中使用退出状态。无需编写 MoonBit 代码。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:7
msgid "From the repository root, with the MoonBit toolchain installed:"
msgstr "在仓库根目录下，已安装 MoonBit 工具链："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:17
msgid "The file contains one theorem:"
msgstr "该文件包含一个定理："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:23
msgid "`moon run src/cmd` builds and runs the tool. Arguments for the tool itself go after `--`, as in `moon run src/cmd -- -d <file>`; once built as a standalone executable, the same call is `qed-cmd -d <file>`."
msgstr "`moon run src/cmd` 构建并运行该工具。工具自身的参数写在 `--` 之后，例如 `moon run src/cmd -- -d <file>`；构建为独立可执行文件后，等价调用为 `qed-cmd -d <file>`。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:25
#: manual/tutorial/elab.md:36
#: manual/tutorial/kernel.md:37
#: manual/tutorial/logic.md:29
#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:30
#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:35
#: manual/tutorial/research_rewrite.md:42
#: manual/tutorial/tactics.md:43
msgid "Everyday tasks"
msgstr "日常任务"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:27
msgid "Check several theorems"
msgstr "检查多个定理"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:29
msgid "Separate theorems with a line containing `qed`. `examples/multi_theorems.qed`:"
msgstr "用只含 `qed` 的一行分隔定理。`examples/multi_theorems.qed`："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:56
msgid "The exit status is 0."
msgstr "退出状态为 0。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:58
msgid "See what was proved"
msgstr "查看证明了什么"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:60
msgid "`-d` prints the conclusion of each theorem, in the kernel's structural notation:"
msgstr "`-d` 以内核的结构化记法打印每个定理的结论："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:70
msgid "For larger goals the conclusion is long, because connectives are printed as their definitions."
msgstr "对于较大的目标，结论会很长，因为联结词是按其定义打印的。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:72
msgid "Read an error"
msgstr "读懂错误"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:74
msgid "`examples/bad_branch.qed` tries to prove the left branch `x` of `x ∨ x` with `truth`:"
msgstr "`examples/bad_branch.qed` 试图用 `truth` 证明 `x ∨ x` 的左分支 `x`："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:94
msgid "Step 3 is `exact truth`; the goal there is `x` under the hypothesis `x`, with the local `h`. Replacing `exact truth` with `exact h` proves the theorem. The exit status is 1."
msgstr "第 3 步是 `exact truth`；此处的目标是假设 `x` 下的 `x`，带有局部变量 `h`。将 `exact truth` 换成 `exact h` 即可证明该定理。退出状态为 1。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:96
msgid "Leave a hole and keep going"
msgstr "留下 hole 并继续"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:98
msgid "`hole` marks a gap. The tool reports it as a warning and checks the remaining theorems. `examples/multi_with_hole.qed`:"
msgstr "`hole` 标记一处缺口。工具将其报告为警告，并继续检查其余定理。`examples/multi_with_hole.qed`："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:117
msgid "The status is 1, because a file with holes is not finished. During development, allow warnings:"
msgstr "状态为 1，因为含有 hole 的文件尚未完成。开发期间可以允许警告："

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:128
msgid "The output is the same; only the status changes."
msgstr "输出相同，只有状态不同。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:130
#: manual/tutorial/elab.md:98
#: manual/tutorial/kernel.md:196
#: manual/tutorial/logic.md:139
#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:124
#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:127
#: manual/tutorial/research_rewrite.md:123
#: manual/tutorial/tactics.md:148
msgid "Going further"
msgstr "进一步使用"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:132
msgid "**Use it in CI.** Run the tool on each proof file and rely on the status: 0 means every theorem was proved. Leave out `--no-warn` in CI so that holes fail the build."
msgstr "**在 CI 中使用。** 对每个证明文件运行该工具并依赖其状态：0 表示每个定理都已证明。CI 中不要加 `--no-warn`，这样 hole 会使构建失败。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:134
msgid "**Build a standalone binary.** `moon build` produces the tool for the default target; on the native target the executable can be called as `qed-cmd -d --no-warn <file>` without `--`."
msgstr "**构建独立二进制。** `moon build` 为默认目标生成该工具；在 native 目标上，可执行文件可直接以 `qed-cmd -d --no-warn <file>` 调用，无需 `--`。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:136
msgid "**Go beyond the subset.** The tool accepts what the prover accepts: the steps and theorem names listed in the [syntax guide](../syntax.md) and the support matrix of the [user manual](../manual.md). For programmatic use, call the [prover](prover.md) from MoonBit."
msgstr "**超越该子集。** 工具接受证明器 (prover) 所接受的内容：[语法指南](../syntax.md)中列出的步骤和定理名称，以及[用户手册](../manual.md)的支持矩阵。若要以编程方式使用，请在 MoonBit 中调用 [prover](prover.md)。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:138
#: manual/tutorial/elab.md:108
#: manual/tutorial/kernel.md:225
#: manual/tutorial/logic.md:162
#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:143
#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:145
#: manual/tutorial/research_rewrite.md:131
#: manual/tutorial/tactics.md:158
msgid "Common pitfalls"
msgstr "常见陷阱"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:140
msgid "**Forgetting `--` with `moon run`.** `moon run src/cmd -d file` passes `-d` to `moon`, not to the tool."
msgstr "**`moon run` 时忘记 `--`。** `moon run src/cmd -d file` 会把 `-d` 传给 `moon`，而不是该工具。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:141
msgid "**Missing `qed` separators.** In a file with several theorems, a missing `qed` makes the file fail to parse (`error[parse] <file>: offset …: missing qed before next theorem`), and nothing is checked."
msgstr "**缺少 `qed` 分隔符。** 在含多个定理的文件中，缺少 `qed` 会导致文件解析失败（`error[parse] <file>: offset …: missing qed before next theorem`），且不会检查任何内容。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:142
msgid "**Free names.** A goal may only mention header binders such as `(x : bool)`, `T` and `F`; another name is an unknown constant and the theorem fails with `error[sig] <file> (<name>): UnknownConst`."
msgstr "**自由名称。** 目标只能提到头部绑定子，如 `(x : bool)`、`T` 和 `F`；其他名称是未知常量，定理会失败并给出 `error[sig] <file> (<name>): UnknownConst`。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:143
msgid "**Expecting `--no-warn` to hide warnings.** It changes the status only."
msgstr "**以为 `--no-warn` 会隐藏警告。** 它只改变状态。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:144
msgid "**Citing an earlier theorem.** Theorems in a file are independent; `exact before_hole` does not refer to the theorem above."
msgstr "**引用前面的定理。** 文件中的定理相互独立；`exact before_hole` 并不指向上面的定理。"

#: manual/tutorial/cmd.md:146
#: manual/tutorial/elab.md:115
#: manual/tutorial/kernel.md:234
#: manual/tutorial/logic.md:170
#: manual/tutorial/parser.md:152
#: manual/tutorial/prover.md:153
#: manual/tutorial/research_rewrite.md:138
